    "cli/internal/cli/runtime_receipt_delivery_test.go": {
      "category": "rewrite",
      "reason": "Reasoned rather than left bare, because this row reads like a coordinated one and is not (#663 added the file; #657 and #661 built the coordinated set). The single occurrence is a path segment inside a fixture string at line 107, `.synaptory/.orchestrator/spq/cycles/009-abcd1234/workstreams/api/receipts/WU-009-qe.json`, and the case it feeds asserts that a filed receipt lands at the ENVELOPE's path rather than at an adapter-side constant. That assertion is path-agnostic: it compares the filed path to the envelope's own, so any nested relative path proves it and this one carries no contract. The file spells neither `workstream_id` nor `WorkstreamID`, so it is outside the signed-field group. It is `rewrite` and not `coordinated` because the segment names no live layout to coordinate with: `spq_paths.py` produces no `workstreams/` level (`execution_state_path`, `receipts_dir` and `tracker_data_path` all sit directly under `cycle_root`), nothing in the tree ever creates one, ADR-035 section 8 decided there is no state migration and that the board reader refuses the old layout by name, and three live assertions already require the segment to be absent (`plugin-codex/tests/test_codex_mcp.py:818`, `api/tests/test_cycle_analytics.py:234`, `e2e/scenarios/test_18_spq_cycle.py:407`). `core/lib/story_pipeline.py:5476` is the one place that still spells the segment in code, and it is a read-side tolerance scan in `companion_receipt_dirs` guarded by `os.path.isdir`, which finds a pre-SPD-194 tree if one is already on disk and never writes one. So the string models a shape the product does not write, and rewriting it makes the case more accurate rather than less.",
